<p>President Donald Trump said member states of his newly created “Board of Peace” have pledged more than $5 billion to support humanitarian aid and reconstruction in Gaza. He said a formal announcement will come when the board holds its inaugural meeting in Washington on Thursday, February 19. Several outlets put the figure at “more than $5 billion,” while one report cited $6 billion. Trump also said participating states have committed “thousands of personnel” to a UN-authorized International Stabilisation Force and local police, intended to help maintain security in the Gaza Strip. The claims come as a ceasefire remains in place, though some reports say Israeli airstrikes and shootings in Gaza have continued. If the pledges are delivered, they would bring new resources and a clearer push for international coordination on day-to-day safety and rebuilding. But key details are still missing from public reporting, including which countries are contributing, how the money would be disbursed, and the force’s exact mandate and makeup.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/N6-72oNo5EZAC7UgjcgzFUwYy6fDxDPzgLz4bIIiHjnmZwiiUduKhgpxRcyO9J7a4HXAF_WLeX94ujqySp1j2zgcm9P0IBNjPdpG6ePD1u_J' alt='US President Donald Trump speaks with members of the media in Palm Beach, Florida, in November 2025 (file photo).' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Meeting venue: Trump said the Board will meet at the Donald J. Trump Institute of Peace in Washington on February 19, 2026.</li><li>Board leadership framing: Trump said it was his honour to serve as the Board’s chairman and called it “the most consequential International Body in History”.</li><li>Hamas disarmament: Trump called for Hamas to begin “full and immediate” disarmament/demilitarization as part of the initiative.</li><li>Pakistan attendance: Pakistan’s Foreign Office spokesperson said Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif will attend the Board meeting, along with Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Ishaq Dar.</li><li>Corroboration note: Only Dawn’s reporting in this source packet says the Board of Peace was proposed in September 2025; the other linked reports here focus on Trump’s Feb. 15 post and the planned Feb. 19 meeting.</li></ul><blockquote>We will announce that member states have pledged more than $5 billion dollars toward the Gaza humanitarian and reconstruction efforts, and have committed thousands of personnel to the International Stabilisation Force and local police to maintain security and peace for Gazans. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: He cast the Board of Peace as a historic international body, said he will serve as its chairman, and tied the initiative to a demand that Hamas demilitarize. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1973450/board-of-peace-members-have-committed-thousands-of-personnel-to-gaza-force-trump'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>RT: RT highlighted Trump’s claims of a large troop deployment to Gaza and framed the effort as a “humanitarian” initiative. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/632592-trump-peace-board-thousands-troops/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/trump-says-his-board-of-peace-members-pledged-5-billion-for-gaza-11008215#publisher=newsstand'>Trump Says His Board Of Peace Members Pledged $5 Billion For Gaza</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/board-of-peace-members-have-pledged-5-billion-for-gaza-trump/article70636197.ece'>Board of Peace members have pledged $5 billion for Gaza: Trump</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/632592-trump-peace-board-thousands-troops/'>Trump’s Board of Peace rallies ‘thousands’ of troops for Gaza deployment</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/trump-board-of-peace-backers-pledge-5-billion-for-gaza/a-75982195'>Trump: &#x27;Board of Peace&#x27; backers pledge $5 Billion for Gaza</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/trump-says-